<!-- MINDONE 15.09: remove the keyboard's own bottom padding (requirement: "take the emptiness below
     the keyboard away").

     Two separate gaps sit under the bottom key row, and both had to go:
       1. the navigation bar inset - handled in the framework dimens overlay, which sets
          navigation_bar_frame_height to 0 while keeping the gesture area;
       2. this one, LatinIME's own padding, applied through themes-common.xml as
          keyboardBottomPadding -> @fraction/config_keyboard_bottom_padding_holo.

     Stock is 4.669%p of the keyboard height. On our 150dp keyboard that is ~7dp of dead space
     under the last row - small on a normal phone, but this screen only has 523dp of usable
     height (F4014), so it is worth reclaiming. Zero puts the bottom row against the screen edge,
     which is exactly the intent.

     If the bottom row ever feels too easy to mis-hit at the very edge, 1-2%p is the middle
     ground; the keyboard height itself is next door in dimens.xml.
-->
<resources>
    <fraction name="config_keyboard_bottom_padding_holo">0%p</fraction>
</resources>
